o put all the changeling stuff into it then that's going to be a lot more work.<br /> <br /> But nothing says it can't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T20:29:00-07:00","id":1197019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1196903-chimera-fetishes?p=1196925#post1196925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends how deep into changeling lore you want to dive. If you just want to use a chimera spirit, I wouldn't see the harm in it. Just treat it like any other spirit in terms of relationship, alliance, and what not. If you want to put all the changeling stuff into it then that's going to be a lot more work.<br /> <br /> But nothing says it can't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Chimera aren't spirits? I mean you can't bind a infomorph from the Digital web into a fetish either...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T23:14:57-07:00","id":1197054,"title":"","content":"I remember some what a npc in one of the changeling supplements being a Mage whose all hopped up in fae culture including having a wonder/treasure that is chimerical in nature thats a klingon/dwarven laser crossbow? As stated above it really depends how deep in changeling lore you wanna go, Mages can touch on the astral umbra and the dreamings umbral reflection and find spirits that fill such niches. You could use those spirit stats to reflect the chimera you're trying to bind. Spirits of Love might be Leanan Sidhe who visits a dreamer to gain glamour from their collective nights spent, spirit of vices might fill the niche of dragons or foul fae creatures if needed, also the wyld has a few spirits in its following that can be described as fae in nature like Goblins, Gremlins, and even at a stretch Mothman if your wanna lump them into the world of chimerical things. <br /> <br /> Also lets not forget a Mages Quiet when external manifest Chimerically so that nagging voice in your head now coming out of the motley of madness spun monster following you can and do affect changelings and chimeras. This is one reason changelings try and avoid Magi from the traditions outside of general problems from what I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date"